{"name":"Deer Leather","hex":"#ac7434","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"deer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ruminant mammal with hooves and often antlers, of the family Cervidae, or one of several similar animals from related families of the order Artiodactyla, such as the musk deer or mouse deer.","Such a mammal that is in the family Cervidae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deer"},{"term":"leather","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tough material produced from the skin of animals, by tanning or similar process, used e.g. for clothing; often denotes leather from cattle when no qualifier specifies otherwise.","A piece of the above used for polishing."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of leather.","Referring to one who wears leather clothing (motorcycle jacket, chaps over 501 jeans, boots), especially as a sign of sadomasochistic homosexuality."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leather"}],"entries":[{"title":"Deer","blocks":[{"text":"A deer or true deer is a hoofed ruminant ungulate of the family Cervidae. Cervidae is divided into subfamilies Cervinae and Capreolinae. Male deer of almost all species, as well as female reindeer, grow and shed new antlers each year. These antlers are bony extensions of the skull and are often used for combat between males."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Family_Cervidae_five_species.jpg/330px-Family_Cervidae_five_species.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deer"},{"title":"Leather","blocks":[{"text":"Leather is a strong, flexible and durable material obtained from the tanning, or chemical treatment, of animal skins and hides to prevent decay. The most common leathers come from cattle, sheep, goats, equine animals, buffalo, pigs and hogs, ostriches, and aquatic animals such as seals and alligators."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Leathertools.jpg/330px-Leathertools.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leather"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Cervidae_distribution.png/500px-Cervidae_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Cervidae_distribution.png/1280px-Cervidae_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Cervidae_distribution.png/500px-Cervidae_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACervidae_distribution.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Lucas_Cranach_d.%C3%84._-_Hirschjagd_des_Kurf%C3%BCrsten_Friedrich_des_Weisen_%28Kunsthistorisches_Museum%29.jpg/500px-Lucas_Cranach_d.%C3%84._-_Hirschjagd_des_Kurf%C3%BCrsten_Friedrich_des_Weisen_%28Kunsthistorisches_Museum%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Lucas_Cranach_d.%C3%84._-_Hirschjagd_des_Kurf%C3%BCrsten_Friedrich_des_Weisen_%28Kunsthistorisches_Museum%29.jpg/1280px-Lucas_Cranach_d.%C3%84._-_Hirschjagd_des_Kurf%C3%BCrsten_Friedrich_des_Weisen_%28Kunsthistorisches_Museum%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Lucas_Cranach_d.%C3%84._-_Hirschjagd_des_Kurf%C3%BCrsten_Friedrich_des_Weisen_%28Kunsthistorisches_Museum%29.jpg/500px-Lucas_Cranach_d.%C3%84._-_Hirschjagd_des_Kurf%C3%BCrsten_Friedrich_des_Weisen_%28Kunsthistorisches_Museum%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"The Stag Hunt 